'''''Nothoscordum'' × ''borbonicum''''', also known as '''honeybells''',<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |accessdate=2014-10-17 }}</ref> '''fragrant false garlic'''<ref>{{PLANTS|id=NOBO|taxon=Nothoscordum borbonicum|accessdate=20 July 2015}}</ref> and '''onion weed''', is a [[bulbous]] [[Perennial plant|perennial]].  It has become [[Naturalisation (biology)|naturalized]] as a nearly [[Cosmopolitan distribution|cosmopolitan]] [[weed]].<ref name="rahn1998">Knud Rahn. 1998. "Alliaceae" pages 70-78. In: Klaus Kubitzki (editor). ''The Families and Genera of Vascular Plants'' volume III. Springer-Verlag: Berlin;Heidelberg, Germany. {{ISBN|978-3-540-64060-8}}</ref> The whitish [[flower]]s are sweetly scented. It is a hybrid between ''[[Nothoscordum entrerianum|N. entrerianum]]'' and ''[[Nothoscordum gracile|N. gracile]]''.<ref>{{Citation |contribution=''Nothoscordum'' × ''borbonicum'' |title=World Checklist of Selected Plant Families |publisher=The Board of Trustees of the [[Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew]] |url=http://apps.kew.org/wcsp/namedetail.do?name_id=282268 |accessdate=2012-02-27 }}</ref>

The [[Binomial nomenclature|binomial]] [[Scientific name|names]] ''Nothoscordum fragrans'' and ''[[Nothoscordum gracile]]'' have also been applied to this plant.<ref name="rahn1998"/>

